# Gemini review gate (required every PR)

**Never merge without a Gemini Code Assist review.** Not for UI-only changes, not for doc-only changes, not because the user is on phone, not because the fix feels urgent.

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md` § Pull request workflow. This rule exists so the gate loads every session via `.cursor/rules/`.

## After every push that opens or updates a PR

1. Open the PR as **draft** unless the user asked otherwise.
2. Check for `gemini-code-assist`:
   ```bash
   gh pr view <number> --json reviews,comments
   gh api repos/elmorshedy-del/ShawqAds/pulls/<number>/reviews
   gh api repos/elmorshedy-del/ShawqAds/pulls/<number>/comments
   ```
3. **No Gemini yet → poll autonomously.** Do not ask the user to check back. Poll up to **5 times** per session (~30–60s apart). On the next session, poll again first if the PR is still open.
4. Fix **critical** and **medium** Gemini feedback; push; re-check reviews/comments.
5. **Only then** mark ready (if draft) and merge.

## Hard stops

- User says "merge it" but Gemini has not reviewed → **still wait** for Gemini (see `AGENTS.md` step 6).
- Skip Gemini **only** when the user explicitly says to skip Gemini for **that specific PR**.

## What to report while waiting

Brief status only, e.g. "PR #49 open — polling for Gemini (attempt 2/5)." Keep polling yourself.

## Why this matters (PR #18)

Gemini caught removed imports that would crash at runtime, plus medium issues in hot loops and types. Treat every review as a required checklist, not optional feedback.
